{
  "rationale": "The plant G models a robot cycling through four square sides, with explicit states for each side and corner. It includes all motion and perception events, and models how obstacle events interrupt or redirect actions. The specification E enforces safe obstacle-aware behavior: move_backward is only allowed from front-obstacle recovery, full_rotate is only a last resort, and after any recovery, the robot returns to the square sequence as soon as possible. All six controllable actions are enabled somewhere, but only one per state. The automata are deterministic and total on uncontrollable events.",
  "strategy": [
    "Explicitly encode each square side and corner as a state, so the robot resumes the correct sequence after recovery.",
    "Obstacle recovery uses short directed turns or brief backward escape; full_rotate is only allowed after repeated failures. After recovery, the robot returns to the square sequence quickly."
  ],
